    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nCurrently LSP hover, diagnostics hover, etc., use a custom floating window. These windows have \"only one-at-a-time\" behavior (quasi-modal). I.e. when the cursor moves, they disappear; and if another one is displayed, the old one disappears.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe preview-window is exactly intended for this quasi-modal UX. We just haven't used it up to now because it didn't have popup/floatwin support https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/26799 .\n\n- Enable 'previewpopup' by default.\n- Use preview-window for LSP hover, diagnostic hover, `:checkhealth` floatwin, ...\n- Deprecate `lsp.util.open_floating_preview` (it should be replaced by `nvim_open_win` features anyway, see https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/25514 )\n\ncc @glepnir \n\nRelated:\n\n- https://github.com/gh-liu/nvim-peek",
